D. SYNTHESIS
============================================================================================================
  1. The LRC condition is exactly a two-sided bracket condition around the stationary vertex:
     left_gap(t) >= 1/n and right_gap(t) >= 1/n.
     All 15 sampled witness rows satisfy this exact local condition.
  2. Quotient ladders preserve more local metric data than max-gap alone records.  Repeated ladder bracket margins:
     n=15, margin=+7/360: n15 d=3 ladder, n15 d=5 ladder
     n=16, margin=+1/176: n16 d=2 ladder, n16 d=4 ladder, n16 d=8 ladder, n16 d=16 ladder
  3. The global nearest-neighbor digraph is extra data, not a substitute for the bracket.
     Positive-gap rows where no moving runner has the stationary runner as its nearest neighbor:
     n14 d=7 ladder, n14 d=14 ladder, n14 window completion, n15 d=3 ladder, n15 d=5 ladder, n15 d=15 ladder, n15 window completion, n16 d=4 ladder, n16 d=16 ladder
  4. Tournament structure enters through the circular order flow.  As t moves, adjacent swaps and half-turn ties change the lex-completed circular tournament; a counterexample would need every such order state to keep at least one of the two stationary bracket gaps below 1/n.
